.SH NAME
Test2::Handle \- Base class for Test2 handles used in V# bundles.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
This is what you interact with when you use the \f(CWT2()\fR function in a test that
uses Test2::V1.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.SS RECOMMENDED
.IX Subsection "RECOMMENDED"
.Vb 1
\&    use Test2::V1;
\&
\&    my $handle = T2();
\&
\&    $handle\->ok(1, "Passing Test");
.Ve
.SS "WITHOUT SUGAR"
.IX Subsection "WITHOUT SUGAR"
.Vb 1
\&    use Test2::Handle();
\&
\&    my $handle = Test2::Handle\->new(base => \*(AqTest2::V1::Base\*(Aq);
\&
\&    $handle\->ok(1, "Passing test");
.Ve
